A '''Separatist outpost''' was a [[CIS mobile command center]] on the [[planet]] [[Maridun]] was used by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]] for weapons testing.

==History==
In [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Confederate]] [[General]] [[Lok Durd]] built the outpost to protect their [[C-9979 landing craft|landing ship]] and it's cargo, the prototype [[Defoliator]] [[Defoliator Deployment Tank|Deployment Tank]]. At the outpost, Durd and his [[technician]] prepared to test the weapon. Durd then had [[battle droid]]s stand at attention in anticipation of the test. Durd asked that two volunteers to step in order to test the weapon's effects on [[droid]]s.<ref name="DoP" />

Durd contacted the Confederate [[Head of State]], [[Count]] [[Dooku]], via [[hologram]] to let him watch the demonstration of the weapon. After it's successful test, Dooku asked Durd to test the weapon on [[Sentience|living beings]], to which the general agreed to carry out on the nearby [[Lurmen]] [[Lurmen village|village]]. Durd then took the majority of his forces to the village and left a small contingent at the outpost.<ref name="DoP" />

Unbeknownst to Durd, [[Jedi General]]s [[Aayla Secura]], [[Anakin Skywalker]], his apprentice [[Ahsoka Tano]], [[Clone Commander|Commander]] [[Bly]], and [[Clone Captain|Captain]] [[Rex]] had recently crash-landed on the [[planet]]. Together they planned to steal the [[shuttle]] and then return to Lurmen Village to protect them against Durd's weapon. Skywalker, Rex and Bly distracted the outside patrols while Secura and Tano scaled the outpost's walls. Together, they were able to [[Defense of Maridun|eliminate]] the remaining droids around the base's [[Separatist command center|command center]] and took the shuttle back to the village, yet not before finding, and taking, several [[Deflector shield generator|shield generators]] the group thought may come useful. The outpost was deserted.<ref name="DoP" />

